Hi , I studied ACID properties in very deep how it supports Transactions and how various problems occur 
While exploring Acid i get confused a lot in Isolation , because isolation do not effect real world operations 
in some cases , still we sees it as a problem . 
LIKE EXAMPLE : there is only one flight ticket is left 
T1 reads the data ticket=1;
T2 reads the data and write it (booked it) commit it.
When T1 again reads data it sees ticket=0. 
so T1 cannot book ticket now because no ticket is available and there is nothing wrong in real worls scenario here. 
but it is not following ISOLATION (NON REPETABLE READ). 

There is a thing called Concurrench Control : it is making multiple transactions running concurrently by 
following ACID proerties 
Without Concurrency Control :
1-> Lost Update 
2-> Dirty Read 
3-> Inconsistent Data 
4-> race condition 
There are Various Technique of Concurrency Control 
1->Locks
2->Serializability 
3->MVCC -Multiversion Concurrency Control 
In modern databases like PostgreSQL and MYSQL MVCC is used highly for Maintaing high concurrency 

